              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Generate Quick Email Content"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_QUICK_EMAIL_CONTENT",
          "id": "1767902281000",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767902281004_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an email copywriting assistant. Generate an engaging email subject line and body based on the information provided below.\n\nThe response including footnote must be written entirely in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.language}}. Ensure the tone, grammar, and phrasing are natural and appropriate for that language.\n\nBusiness Object Context ( {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.boContext}} ):\nThis contains details about the event, product, journey or business object (e.g., Name, Format, Description, CategoryNames, etc.).\nPrompt Context ( {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.promptContext}} ):\nThis indicates the purpose or type of email to generate (e.g., Promotional Email, Follow-up Email, etc.).\nEmail Subject Tokens ( {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailSubjectTokens}} ):\nThese are dynamic fields such as First_Name , Last_Name, Full_Name and Work_Email etc to personalize the email subject.For each dynamic field, output the token as $[token_name] for example, ${First_Name}, matching the case and spelling of each entry in the email_subject_tokens list. Only use tokens from the provided email_subject_tokens array and use all the tokens.  All these tokens are recipient's information.\nEmail Body Tokens ( {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailBodyTokens}} ):\nThese are dynamic fields such as First_Name , Last_Name, Full_Name and Work_Email etc to personalize the email body.For each dynamic field, output the token as ${token_name} for example, ${First_Name} matching the case and spelling of each entry in the email_body_tokens list. Only use tokens from the provided email_body_tokens array and use all the tokens.  All these tokens are recipient's information.\nUser Prompt ( {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userPrompt}} ):\nThis is an optional instruction from the user for tailoring the tone or style (e.g., make the email informal, highlight networking, etc.).\nFoot Note ( {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.footnote}} ):\nThis is an optional instruction from the user for adding a footnote. If provided, always insert the footnote content exactly as per Language  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.language}}—without modification, omission, or enhancement—at the end of the email body. Do not precede it with the word \"Footnote\" or any other label. (e.g., If you’ve already registered, please ignore this email — we look forward to seeing you at the event!).\n\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON array with objects containing only \"subject\" and \"body\" fields, as in the example below:\n{\n  \"subject\": \"Join Us at the Tech Symposium – Let’s Make It a Day to Remember!\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi ${First_Name} ${Last_Name},\\n\\nWe’re thrilled to invite you to our annual Tech Symposium! This event is a fantastic opportunity for you, ${Full_Name}, to connect with industry peers and expand your knowledge.\\n\\nFor your records, please note that this email is also your receipt, sent to: ${Work_Email}.\\n\\nIf you have any questions, don't hesitate to reach out. If you’ve already registered, please ignore this email — we look forward to seeing you at the event!\\n\\nBest regards,\\nThe Organizing Team\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"body\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
